chx:X_RefusedRecipients a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:RefusedRecipients ; rdfs:label "smtplib.SMTPRecipientsRefused"@en ; skos:definition "When the server refused one of two recipients (550) send_message returned a dict naming the refused address and the message was stored for the other; only when every recipient was refused did it raise SMTPRecipientsRefused, and nothing was stored."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch20/research> .
chx:IO_RefusedRecipients a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "(lambda g: (exec('import io, os, re, sys, math, shlex, subprocess, json, time, base64, shutil, socket, ssl, smtplib, tempfile, threading, datetime, hashlib, hmac, mimetypes, secrets, warnings, email, inspect, contextlib, importlib.metadata as md\\nfrom datetime import datetime as DT, timedelta as TD, date as D, timezone, UTC\\nfrom zoneinfo import ZoneInfo\\nfrom email import policy, utils as eu\\nfrom email.message import EmailMessage\\nfrom email.mime.text import MIMEText\\nfrom email.mime.multipart import MIMEMultipart\\ndef err(f):\\n    try: return (\\'ok\\', f())\\n    except BaseException as e: return (type(e).__name__, str(e))\\ndef wd():\\n    d = tempfile.mkdtemp(); os.chdir(d); return d\\ndef mk(**kw):\\n    m = EmailMessage(); m[\\'From\\'] = kw.get(\\'frm\\', \\'Al Sweigart <al@example.com>\\'); m[\\'To\\'] = kw.get(\\'to\\', \\'Jon Doe <jon@example.org>\\'); m[\\'Subject\\'] = kw.get(\\'subj\\', \\'RoboCop\\')\\n    m[\\'Date\\'] = eu.formatdate(1797000528, usegmt=True); m[\\'Message-ID\\'] = \\'<fixed-1@example.com>\\'\\n    for k, v in kw.get(\\'extra\\', {}).items(): m[k] = v\\n    m.set_content(kw.get(\\'body\\', \\'Do you want to watch RoboCop this weekend?\\')); return m\\nimport ipaddress, logging\\nlogging.getLogger(\\'mail.log\\').setLevel(logging.CRITICAL)\\nfrom aiosmtpd.controller import Controller\\nfrom aiosmtpd.smtp import AuthResult, LoginPassword\\nfrom cryptography import x509\\nfrom cryptography.x509.oid import NameOID\\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives import hashes, serialization\\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives.asymmetric import ec\\ndef serve(**kw):\\n    d = tempfile.mkdtemp(); key = ec.generate_private_key(ec.SECP256R1()); nm = x509.Name([x509.NameAttribute(NameOID.COMMON_NAME, \\'localhost\\')]); t0 = datetime.datetime(2026, 1, 1)\\n    crt = (x509.CertificateBuilder().subject_name(nm).issuer_name(nm).public_key(key.public_key()).serial_number(1