chx:X_UmbrellaReminder a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:UmbrellaReminder ; rdfs:label "probabilityOfPrecipitation"@en ; skos:definition "Searching the text of a forecast for the word rain found it in neither of 2 sample periods, so it missed the period with a precipitation chance of 60 (Chance Showers And Thunderstorms) that a comparison with a limit of 40 flagged; api.weather.gov answered the point lookup for Chicago and its forecast with periods that carry shortForecast and probabilityOfPrecipitation (a number from 0 to 100 in each of the 14 periods), a number to compare, where the chapter's scraping of weather.gov gives text."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch20/research> .
chx:IO_UmbrellaReminder a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "(lambda g: (exec('import io, os, re, sys, math, shlex, subprocess, json, time, base64, shutil, socket, ssl, smtplib, tempfile, threading, datetime, hashlib, hmac, mimetypes, secrets, warnings, email, inspect, contextlib, importlib.metadata as md\\nfrom datetime import datetime as DT, timedelta as TD, date as D, timezone, UTC\\nfrom zoneinfo import ZoneInfo\\nfrom email import policy, utils as eu\\nfrom email.message import EmailMessage\\nfrom email.mime.text import MIMEText\\nfrom email.mime.multipart import MIMEMultipart\\ndef err(f):\\n    try: return (\\'ok\\', f())\\n    except BaseException as e: return (type(e).__name__, str(e))\\ndef wd():\\n    d = tempfile.mkdtemp(); os.chdir(d); return d\\nPERIODS = [{\\'name\\': \\'Today\\', \\'shortForecast\\': \\'Chance Showers And Thunderstorms\\', \\'detailedForecast\\': \\'A chance of showers and thunderstorms. Sunny.\\', \\'probabilityOfPrecipitation\\': {\\'unitCode\\': \\'wmoUnit:percent\\', \\'value\\': 60}},\\n           {\\'name\\': \\'Tonight\\', \\'shortForecast\\': \\'Mostly Cloudy\\', \\'detailedForecast\\': \\'Mostly cloudy, with a low around 50.\\', \\'probabilityOfPrecipitation\\': {\\'unitCode\\': \\'wmoUnit:percent\\', \\'value\\': None}}]\\ndef naive(p): return \\'rain\\' in (p[\\'shortForecast\\'] + p[\\'detailedForecast\\']).lower()\\ndef better(p, limit=40): return (p[\\'probabilityOfPrecipitation\\'][\\'value\\'] or 0) >= limit\\nout = ([naive(p) for p in PERIODS], [better(p) for p in PERIODS], [p[\\'probabilityOfPrecipitation\\'][\\'value\\'] for p in PERIODS], PERIODS[0][\\'probabilityOfPrecipitation\\'][\\'value\\'] or 0)', g), g['out'])[1])({}) evaluates to ([False, False], [True, False], [60, None], 60)"@en ; chx:input "(lambda g: (exec('import io, os, re, sys, math, shlex, subprocess, json, time, base64, shutil, socket, ssl, smtplib, tempfile, threading, datetime, hashlib, hmac, mimetypes, secrets, warnings, email, inspect, contextlib, importlib.metadata as md\\nfrom datetime import datetime as DT, timedelta as TD, date as D, timezone, UTC\\nfrom zoneinfo import ZoneInfo\\nfrom email import policy, utils as eu\\nfrom email.message import EmailMessage\\nfrom email.mime.text import MIMEText\\nfrom email.mime.multipart import MIMEMultipart\\ndef err(f):\\n    try: return (\\'ok\\', f())\\n    except BaseException as e: return (type(e).__name__, str(e))\\ndef wd():\\n    d = tempfile.mkdtemp(); os.chdir(d); return d\\nPERIODS = [{\\'name\\': \\'Today\\', \\'shortForecast\\': \\'Chance Showers And Thunderstorms\\', \\'detailedForecast\\': \\'A chance of showers and thunderstorms. Sunny.\\', \\'probabilityOfPrecipitation\\': {\\'unitCode\\': \\'wmoUnit:percent\\', \\'value\\': 60}},\\n           {\\'name\\': \\'Tonight\\', \\'shortForecast\\': \\'Mostly Cloudy\\', \\'detailedForecast\\': \\'Mostly cloudy, with a low around 50.\\', \\'probabilityOfPrecipitation\\': {\\'unitCode\\': \\'wmoUnit:percent\\', \\'value\\': None}}]\\ndef naive(p): return \\'rain\\' in (p[\\'shortForecast\\'] + p[\\'detailedForecast\\']).lower()\\ndef better(p, limit=40): return (p[\\'probabilityOfPrecipitation\\'][\\'value\\'] or 0) >= limit\\nout = ([naive(p) for p in PERIODS], [better(p) for p in PERIODS], [p[\\'probabilityOfPrecipitation\\'][\\'value\\'] for p in PERIODS], PERIODS[0][\\'probabilityOfPrecipitation\\'][\\'value\\'] or 0)', g), g['out'])[1])({})" ; chx:output "([False, False], [True, False], [60, None], 60)" .
chx:X_UmbrellaReminder rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_UmbrellaReminder .
chx:X_AutoUnsubscriber a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:AutoUnsubscriber ; rdfs:label "List-Unsubscribe"@en ; skos:definition "Scanning HTML with html.parser for links whose text says unsubscribe found 1 of 3 candidates (the image link and the link that says opt out were missed), the word occurs 2 times in the HTML, and the List-Unsubscribe header (RFC 2369) with List-Unsubscribe-Post (RFC 8058) gave a mailto: and an https: address without parsing any HTML; opening a link with a browser confirms the address is read."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch20/research> .
chx:IO_AutoUnsubscriber a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "(lambda g: (exec('import io, os, re, sys, math, shlex, subprocess, json, time, base64, shutil, socket, ssl, smtplib, tempfile, threading, datetime, hashlib, hmac, mimetypes, secrets, warnings, email, inspect, contextlib, importlib.metadata as md\\nfrom datetime import datetime as DT, timedelta as TD, date as D, timezone, UTC\\nfrom zoneinfo import ZoneInfo\\nfrom email import policy, utils as eu\\nfrom email.message import EmailMessage\\nfrom email.mime.text import MIMEText\\nfrom email.mime.multipart import MIMEMultipart\\ndef err(f):\\n    try: return (\\'ok\\', f())\\n    except BaseException as e: return (type(e).__name__, str(e))\\ndef wd():\\n    d = tempfile.mkdtemp(); os.chdir(d); return d\\nfrom html.parser import HTMLParser\\nHTML = \\'<p>Hi <a href=\\x22https://example.com/u?id=1\\x22>Unsubscribe</a> | <a href=\\x22https://example.com/p\\x22>Preferences</a> | <a href=\\x22https://example.com/x\\x22><img alt=\\x22unsubscribe\\x22></a> <a href=\\x22https://example.com/u2\\x22>click here to opt out</a></p>\\'\\nclass P(HTMLParser):\\n    def __init__(s): super().__init__(); s.cur = None; s.found = []; s.txt = \\'\\'\\n    def handle_starttag(s, tag, attrs):\\n        if tag == \\'a\\': s.cur = dict(attrs).get(\\'href\\'); s.txt = \\'\\'\\n    def handle_data(s, d):\\n        if s.cur: s.txt += d\\n    def handle_endtag(s, tag):\\n        if tag == \\'a\\':\\n            if s.cur and \\'unsubscribe\\' in s.txt.lower(): s.found.append(s.cur)\\n            s.cur = None\\np = P(); p.feed(HTML)\\nm = EmailMessage(); m[\\'List-Unsubscribe\\'] = \\'<mailto:unsub@example.com?subject=unsubscribe>, <https://example.com/u?id=1>\\'; m[\\'List-Unsubscribe-Post\\'] = \\'List-Unsubscribe=One-Click\\'\\nlu = [x.strip(\\'<>\\') for x in m[\\'List-Unsubscribe\\'].split(\\', \\')]\\nout = (p.found, lu, m[\\'List-Unsubscribe-Post\\'], len(re.findall(r\\'unsubscribe\\', HTML, re.I)), [u for u in lu if u.startswith(\\'https://\\')])', g), g['out'])[1])({}) evaluates to (['https://example.com/u?id=1'], ['mailto:unsub@example.com?subject=unsubscribe', 'https://example.com/u?id=1'], 'List-Unsubscribe=One-Click', 2, ['https://example.com/u?id=1'])"@en ; chx:input "(lambda g: (exec('import io, os, re, sys, math, shlex, subprocess, json, time, base64, shutil, socket, ssl, smtplib, tempfile, threading, datetime, hashlib, hmac, mimetypes, secrets, warnings, email, inspect, contextlib, importlib.metadata as md\\nfrom datetime import datetime as DT, timedelta as TD, date as D, timezone, UTC\\nfrom zoneinfo import ZoneInfo\\nfrom email import policy, utils as eu\\nfrom email.message import EmailMessage\\nfrom email.mime.text import MIMEText\\nfrom email.mime.multipart import MIMEMultipart\\ndef err(f):\\n    try: return (\\'ok\\', f())\\n    except BaseException as e: return (type(e).__name__, str(e))\\ndef wd():\\n    d = tempfile.mkdtemp(); os.chdir(d); return d\\nfrom html.parser import HTMLParser\\nHTML = \\'<p>Hi <a href=\\x22https://example.com/u?id=1\\x22>Unsubscribe</a> | <a href=\\x22https://example.com/p\\x22>Preferences</a> | <a href=\\x22https://example.com/x\\x22><img alt=\\x22unsubscribe\\x22></a> <a href=\\x22https://example.com/u2\\x22>click here to opt out</a></p>\\'\\nclass P(HTMLParser):\\n    def __init__(s): super().__init__(); s.cur = None; s.found = []; s.txt = \\'\\'\\n    def handle_starttag(s, tag, attrs):\\n        if tag == \\'a\\': s.cur = dict(attrs).get(\\'href\\'); s.txt = \\'\\'\\n    def handle_data(s, d):\\n        if s.cur: s.txt += d\\n    def handle_endtag(s, tag):\\n        if tag == \\'a\\':\\n            if s.cur and \\'unsubscribe\\' in s.txt.lower(): s.found.append(s.cur)\\n            s.cur = None\\np = P(); p.feed(HTML)\\nm = EmailMessage(); m[\\'List-Unsubscribe\\'] = \\'<mailto:unsub@example.com?subject=unsubscribe>, <https://example.com/u?id=1>\\'; m[\\'List-Unsubscribe-Post\\'] = \\'List-Unsubscribe=One-Click\\'\\nlu = [x.strip(\\'<>\\') for x in m[\\'List-Unsubscribe\\'].split(\\', \\')]\\nout = (p.found, lu, m[\\'List-Unsubscribe-Post\\'], len(re.findall(r\\'unsubscribe\\', HTML, re.I)), [u for u in lu if u.startswith(\\'https://\\')])', g), g['out'])[1])({})" ; chx:output "(['https://example.com/u?id=1'], ['mailto:unsub@example.com?subject=unsubscribe', 'https://example.com/u?id=1'], 'List-Unsubscribe=One-Click', 2, ['https://example.com/u?id=1'])" .
chx:X_AutoUnsubscriber rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_AutoUnsubscriber .
chx:X_EmailControlLoop a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:EmailControlLoop ; rdfs:label "hmac.compare_digest(pw, SECRET)"@en ; skos:definition "The Email-Based Computer Control loop checked a password with hmac.compare_digest, ran only commands of an allow-list with Popen and wait (noop exit 0, sleep exit 0), answered bad password for a wrong one and refused rm; the book's Popen of qBittorrent raised FileNotFoundError on Linux, and compare_digest of a non-ASCII str raised TypeError."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch20/research> .
chx:IO_EmailControlLoop a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "(lambda g: (exec('import io, os, re, sys, math, shlex, subprocess, json, time, base64, shutil, socket, ssl, smtplib, tempfile, threading, datetime, hashlib, hmac, mimetypes, secrets, warnings, email, inspect, contextlib, importlib.metadata as md\\nfrom datetime import datetime as DT, timedelta as TD, date as D, timezone, UTC\\nfrom zoneinfo import ZoneInfo\\nfrom email import policy, utils as eu\\nfrom email.message import EmailMessage\\nfrom email.mime.text import MIMEText\\nfrom email.mime.multipart import MIMEMultipart\\ndef err(f):\\n    try: return (\\'ok\\', f())\\n    except BaseException as e: return (type(e).__name__, str(e))\\ndef wd():\\n    d = tempfile.mkdtemp(); os.chdir(d); return d\\nSECRET = \\'correct horse\\'; ALLOW = {\\'sleep\\': [sys.executable, \\'-c\\', \\'import time; time.sleep(0.2)\\'], \\'noop\\': [sys.executable, \\'-c\\', \\'pass\\']}\\ndef check(msgs):\\n    done = []\\n    for frm, body in msgs:\\n        pw, _, cmd = body.partition(\\':\\')\\n        if not hmac.compare_digest(pw.encode(), SECRET.encode()): done.append((frm, \\'bad password\\')); continue\\n        if cmd not in ALLOW: done.append((frm, \\'refused \\' + cmd)); continue\\n        p = subprocess.Popen(ALLOW[cmd]); done.append((frm, cmd, p.wait()))\\n    return done\\nr = check([(\\'me@example.com\\', \\'correct horse:noop\\'), (\\'x@example.net\\', \\'guess:noop\\'), (\\'me@example.com\\', \\'correct horse:rm\\'), (\\'me@example.com\\', \\'correct horse:sleep\\')])\\nfnf = err(lambda: subprocess.Popen([\\'C:\\\\\\\\Program Files (x86)\\\\\\\\qBittorrent\\\\\\\\qbittorrent.exe\\', \\'shakespeare_complete_works.torrent\\']))\\nout = (r, fnf[0], hmac.compare_digest(b\\'a\\', b\\'a\\'), err(lambda: hmac.compare_digest(\\'é\\', \\'é\\'))[0])', g), g['out'])[1])({}) evaluates to ([('me@example.com', 'noop', 0), ('x@example.net', 'bad password'), ('me@example.com', 'refused rm'), ('me@example.com', 'sleep', 0)], 'FileNotFoundError', True, 'TypeError')"@en ; chx:input "(lambda g: (exec('import io, os, re, sys, math, shlex, subprocess, json, time, base64, shutil, socket, ssl, smtplib, tempfile, threading, datetime, hashlib, hmac, mimetypes, secrets, warnings, email, inspect, contextlib, importlib.metadata as md\\nfrom datetime import datetime as DT, timedelta as TD, date as D, timezone, UTC\\nfrom zoneinfo import ZoneInfo\\nfrom email import policy, utils as eu\\nfrom email.message import EmailMessage\\nfrom email.mime.text import MIMEText\\nfrom email.mime.multipart import MIMEMultipart\\ndef err(f):\\n    try: return (\\'ok\\', f())\\n    except BaseException as e: return (type(e).__name__, str(e))\\ndef wd():\\n    d = tempfile.mkdtemp(); os.chdir(d); return d\\nSECRET = \\'correct horse\\'; ALLOW = {\\'sleep\\': [sys.executable, \\'-c\\', \\'import time; time.sleep(0.2)\\'], \\'noop\\': [sys.executable, \\'-c\\', \\'pass\\']}\\ndef check(msgs):\\n    done = []\\n    for frm, body in msgs:\\n        pw, _, cmd = body.partition(\\':\\')\\n        if not hmac.compare_digest(pw.encode(), SECRET.encode()): done.append((frm, \\'bad password\\')); continue\\n        if cmd not in ALLOW: done.append((frm, \\'refused \\' + cmd)); continue\\n        p = subprocess.Popen(ALLOW[cmd]); done.append((frm, cmd, p.wait()))\\n    return done\\nr = check([(\\'me@example.com\\', \\'correct horse:noop\\'), (\\'x@example.net\\', \\'guess:noop\\'), (\\'me@example.com\\', \\'correct horse:rm\\'), (\\'me@example.com\\', \\'correct horse:sleep\\')])\\nfnf = err(lambda: subprocess.Popen([\\'C:\\\\\\\\Program Files (x86)\\\\\\\\qBittorrent\\\\\\\\qbittorrent.exe\\', \\'shakespeare_complete_works.torrent\\']))\\nout = (r, fnf[0], hmac.compare_digest(b\\'a\\', b\\'a\\'), err(lambda: hmac.compare_digest(\\'é\\', \\'é\\'))[0])', g), g['out'])[1])({})" ; chx:output "([('me@example.com', 'noop', 0), ('x@example.net', 'bad password'), ('me@example.com', 'refused rm'), ('me@example.com', 'sleep', 0)], 'FileNotFoundError', True, 'TypeError')" .
chx:X_EmailControlLoop rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_EmailControlLoop .
chx:X_SecondEditionContent a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SecondEditionContent ; rdfs:label "smtplib in the 2nd edition"@en ; skos:definition "The 2nd edition's chapter 18, Sending Email and Text Messages, mentions smtplib 21 times, imapclient 20, pyzmail 14 and Twilio 31, while chapter 20 of the 3rd edition names smtplib and imaplib only to say EZGmail is better, and replaces them with the Gmail API, the gateway table and ntfy; observed on 2026-10-13. Recorded in the live observations."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch20/research> .
chx:X_MissingExampleImplementation a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:MissingExampleImplementation ; rdfs:label "an example implementation"@en ; skos:definition "Chapter 20 says that a reader who gets stuck on the Email-Based Computer Control program can download an example implementation from the book page of No Starch Press; the page holds none (0 occurrences of an example implementation, of Email-Based, of ezgmail or of ntfy), the online materials hold 91 files and none for this chapter, and phoneAndEmail.py in them belongs to chapter 8. Recorded in the live observations."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch20/research> .
